<p id="S4.T5.6" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T5.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">Orange</span> = moderately sensitive data; <span id="S4.T5.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF6666;">Red</span> = critically sensitive data.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In numerous instances, the exposed credentials were accompanied by the original login page URL, further escalating the risk by revealing exactly where an attacker could attempt to use them. This analysis highlights that, for as little as $50 using LLM-based analysis—in our case Qwen-2.5 72B—a malicious actor could obtain valuable information.</p>
</div>
